                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "239414683",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198073516577",
                            "num_reviews": 49,
                            "playtime_forever": 1948,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 1777,
                            "playtime_at_review": 1948,
                            "last_played": 1793861575
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Thoughts here at time of True Ending completion (11/5/26).\n\nI bought this over 10 years ago as a bit of a joke since Chris Chan believed he was the C64 CPU and it was on sale. I played the first area then with the horrendous base game graphics and muddy FXAA - that and a general apathy to moe stuff and long-term investment in any JRPG made me resign this as a bad purchase.\nCall it a change of pace from going through other games in my backlog but I felt compelled to atleast try it out again (with a graphics mod called Neptastic that made the graphics clean looking). It started off as a novel interest, but the combo system and expressive (but not Too annoying) voice work actually sunk its teeth into me and I played through the whole damn thing. The music is also pretty dang good (highlights were the Cyber theme and each CPU's themes).\n\nThere wasn't as much grinding as I expected - it's cheeky that you have to use the in-game 'Weaken Enemies' plan to turn off the grind ... except when it still comes up before the fight with the mech/anti-skill&item bots and the final boss as such.\n\nI ended up liking the characters (in a Saturday morning cartoon way) and laughed at the dialogue at a couple of points.\n\nI can't say I'm going to get into the series - even if I got the original Vita release back in the day, I probably still would've stopped at this one - but I'm glad I gave this game a real chance. It paid off. I feel like I have an appreciation for something I never would have expected.\n\nTL;DR - It's bretty good, but during the stone age...",
